    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Neovascular age-related macular degeneration, left eye, dry after loading (H35.3221)</content>. Loading phase complete. Acuity has risen 14 letters (55 to 69) and the macula is dry (central subfield thickness 274 µm), meeting both loading goals. Third injection given today without complication. [S]<list><item>Begin treat-and-extend: next injection in eight weeks, aflibercept&apos;s standard interval after loading.</item><item>Extend by two weeks at each visit while the macula stays dry; shorten if fluid returns.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Intermediate dry age-related macular degeneration, right eye (H35.3112)</content>. Stable. [S]<list><item>Continue the AREDS2 supplement and daily Amsler checks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Best-corrected visual acuity (ETDRS letters)</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left 69 letters, up 14 from baseline; loading goal met</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Optical coherence tomography of the macula</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Left eye dry; central subfield thickness 274 µm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Intraocular pressure before and after injection</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Before injection 14 mmHg left; after injection, optic nerve perfused and counting fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dilated examination of the fellow (right) eye</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Large drusen unchanged; no fluid</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Intravitreal injection safety</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No complication after three injections; last loading dose today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Teaching on warning signs of endophthalmitis and retinal detachment</td><td>Every injection visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed again before the longer interval</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Daily home Amsler grid, each eye</td><td>Daily</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Daily checks recorded; no change in the right eye</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AREDS2 supplement for intermediate AMD</td><td>Daily, long term</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking it daily</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Low-vision rehabilitation, with home fall-risk review and a driving assessment</td><td>Once central vision is reduced; review as vision changes</td><td>Referred</td><td>Evaluation done this month; home visit and driving assessment under way</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>At follow-up, because vision loss raises the risk of depression; periodically at 65 or older</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned at the July primary care review</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Gain at least 10 ETDRS letters in the left eye by the end of the loading phase. Outcome by 2026-05-07: Left eye improved from 55 to 69 letters after three injections [S]</item><item>Dry macula on OCT (central subfield thickness below 300 um, no fluid) by the end of the loading phase. Outcome by 2026-05-07: Central subfield thickness fell from 418 to 274 um with no fluid [S]</item><item>Check the Amsler grid daily for each eye and report any change the same day. In progress; target 2026-07-02 [S]</item><item>Complete a low-vision rehabilitation evaluation and set up studio lighting and magnification by the July visit. In progress; target 2026-07-02 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Age-Related Macular Degeneration Preferred Practice Pattern (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and glaucoma monographs (eye-examination items) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Retina visit in eight weeks, with the primary care review of vision rehabilitation on the same day. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-02: treat-and-extend retina visit and primary care review of vision rehabilitation. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
